<div class="header">
  <div class="dateline">Prepared October 2026 &middot; Sources as of FY 2026&ndash;27</div>
  <h1>Where State, County &amp; City Priorities Align in Santa Fe</h1>
  <p>A map of shared priorities across three levels of government &mdash; and where community listening bridges the gaps that remain.</p>

  <div class="finding">
    <p><strong>The headline finding:</strong> on five of the ten highest-priority issues facing Santa Fe &mdash; housing &amp; homelessness, behavioral health, public safety, children &amp; families, and the workforce economy &mdash; the State, the County and the City are already aligned, each with dedicated FY2026&ndash;27 funding or legislation behind it. The money and the political will are there.</p>
    <p>What's missing at every level, on nearly every issue, is the same thing: a structured way to hear from the residents those dollars are meant to serve before the plans are finalized. That gap &mdash; not a lack of government attention &mdash; is where Creative Santa Fe's community listening model has room to work, issue after issue, regardless of how aligned the three governments already are.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="legend">
