      <div class="bridge-box">
        <div class="bridge-icon">&#9670;</div>
        <div class="bridge-text"><strong>CrSF bridge opportunity:</strong> The state leans toward enforcement; the city and county are also investing in alternative response. Residents have strong views on this tension but few forums to express them. A listening event can help policymakers understand what "safety" means to different neighborhoods &mdash; and build legitimacy for whichever approach a community supports.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. Children, Youth & Families -->
  <div class="issue-card" id="youth">
    <div class="issue-header" onclick="toggle(this)">
      <div class="issue-rank full">4</div>
      <div class="issue-title-area">
        <h2>Children, Youth &amp; Families</h2>
        <div class="issue-subtitle">Universal childcare and youth crisis services converge</div>
      </div>
      <svg class="chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 8l5 5 5-5"/></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="issue-body">
      <div class="govt-columns">
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-state)"></span> NM State</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>$160M+ for universal child care (infant&ndash;age 12)</li>
            <li>Independent Child Protection Authority</li>
            <li>Double foster/kinship stipends to $900/mo</li>
            <li>$50M/yr Indian Education Fund</li>
            <li>180-day school year funding; cell phone ban</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">2025&ndash;26 State of the State</div>
        </div>
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-county)"></span> SF County</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Youth Behavioral Health Center development</li>
            <li>Youth crisis services &amp; case management</li>
            <li>Services targeting young girls &amp; LGBTQ youth</li>
            <li>Joint working group on childcare with City</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">FY24&ndash;26 Health Action Plan</div>
        </div>
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-city)"></span> City of Santa Fe</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Childcare as a guaranteed right (legislative)</li>
            <li>Early childhood education expansion</li>
            <li>Youth gun violence intervention</li>
            <li>Family Navigator (FFN) stipends &amp; apprenticeships</li>
            <li>Fresh food for school &amp; senior meals</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">2026 Legislative Priorities</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bridge-box">
        <div class="bridge-icon">&#9670;</div>
        <div class="bridge-text"><strong>CrSF bridge opportunity:</strong> Parents and caregivers know where the system breaks &mdash; which neighborhoods have no childcare, which youth are falling through the cracks, what "accessible" really means for working families. Community listening here gives policymakers the on-the-ground picture that data alone can't provide.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. Workforce & Economy -->
  <div class="issue-card" id="economy">
    <div class="issue-header" onclick="toggle(this)">
      <div class="issue-rank full">5</div>
      <div class="issue-title-area">
        <h2>Workforce &amp; Economic Development</h2>
        <div class="issue-subtitle">State goes big-ticket; city and county focus on local workforce</div>
      </div>
      <svg class="chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 8l5 5 5-5"/></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="issue-body">
      <div class="govt-columns">
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-state)"></span> NM State</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>$150M tax credits for quantum computing &amp; fusion</li>
            <li>150,000 jobs added over 7 years</li>
            <li>3rd nationally in new business applications</li>
            <li>$20M for business expansion/relocation</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">2026 State of the State</div>
        </div>
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-county)"></span> SF County</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Workforce development via reentry programs</li>
            <li>SF Community College training partnerships</li>
            <li>Broadband expansion (federal grant pursuit)</li>
            <li>On-site job placement at detention facility</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">Strategic Plan &amp; BH Reform Plan</div>
        </div>
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-city)"></span> City of Santa Fe</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>7-area economic development strategy</li>
            <li>Phase 2 strategic plan launch (2025)</li>
            <li>Broadband &amp; WiFi access expansion</li>
            <li>Economic mobility programs</li>
            <li>Midtown Redevelopment ($10M infrastructure)</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">Economic Development Office &amp; Leg. Priorities</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bridge-box">
        <div class="bridge-icon">&#9670;</div>
        <div class="bridge-text"><strong>CrSF bridge opportunity:</strong> The state's big bets (quantum, fusion, tech credits) may not connect to what Santa Feans need for economic stability. Community listening can surface what workforce training, business support, and broadband access look like for residents who aren't in the tech pipeline &mdash; and whether growth strategies match the community they serve.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 6. Climate & Environment -->
  <div class="issue-card" id="climate">
