      <div class="issue-title-area">
        <h2>Climate &amp; Environment</h2>
        <div class="issue-subtitle">State and City leading; County focused on fleet electrification</div>
      </div>
      <svg class="chevron" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 8l5 5 5-5"/></svg>
    </div>
    <div class="issue-body">
      <div class="govt-columns">
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-state)"></span> NM State</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Codify Climate Action Plan (45% cut by 2030)</li>
            <li>Net-zero emissions by 2050</li>
            <li>Affordability commission for clean energy transition</li>
            <li>Forest management &amp; strategic water supply</li>
            <li>State fire insurance program</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">2025&ndash;26 State of the State</div>
        </div>
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-county)"></span> SF County</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>EV fleet policy &amp; charger installation</li>
            <li>Climate health awareness campaigns</li>
            <li>Humanitarian Action Plan for heat events</li>
            <li>Cooling centers for vulnerable residents</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">Health Action Plan &amp; Strategic Plan</div>
        </div>
        <div class="govt-col">
          <h3><span class="h-dot" style="background:var(--accent-city)"></span> City of Santa Fe</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Building electrification &amp; renewable energy</li>
            <li>Forest fire mitigation &amp; watershed restoration</li>
            <li>Complete streets &amp; emissions inspection</li>
            <li>Extended producer responsibility &amp; recycling</li>
            <li>Water reuse legislation</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="source">2026 Legislative Priorities</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bridge-box">
        <div class="bridge-icon">&#9670;</div>
        <div class="bridge-text"><strong>CrSF bridge opportunity:</strong> Climate policy often splits along economic lines &mdash; clean energy transition and affordability are real tensions in a state that depends on oil and gas revenue. Listening events can surface what residents need to feel confident in the transition: job retraining, energy cost protections, wildfire preparedness in their neighborhood.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

